5. ATM Transaction Sequence Simulation

1. Problem Statement
Simulate a series of deposits and withdrawals, update an account balance, reject invalid or unaffordable withdrawals,
and summarize accepted and rejected transactions.

2. Objectives
•	Update balance after each transaction.
•	Reject invalid amounts and withdrawals exceeding balance.
•	Report final balance and transaction counts.

3. Assumptions
•	Opening balance is ₹5,000.
•	Transactions are tuples of type and amount.
•	Withdrawal limit per transaction is ₹3,000.
•	Amounts must be positive.

4. Algorithm
1. Set the opening balance and counters.
2. Process each transaction tuple.
3. Accept deposits with positive amounts.
4. Accept withdrawals only if within limit and balance.
5. Print each decision and final summary.

